I had wishless and polyselfless for a looong time, up until after I got
the actual Amulet.  But I ran into Rodney and he stole my only source
of Magic Resistance, and I had to choose between giving up the conduct
or dying.  And since I was giving up the conduct, I figured I might as
well use the THREE /oW's in my possession to their fullest.  Somewhere
around my trouble with Rodney I had my brain eaten and then
accidentally drank an un-ID'd potion of polymorph, and BAM, there went
polyselfless (as well as my robe and Hawaaian shirt, which I ended up
using wishes on to get back).  Also, at some point I accidentally
polymorphed ONE item, though I don't ever recall zapping a wand of
polymorph.  Maybe I dipped something into a potion of polymorph?
Anyway, my final conducts were genoless, polypileless, and farmless,
and my failed conducts were polyitemless, wishless, and polyselfless.

What have I learned?  Don't ever trust a quest artifact as your only
source of ANYTHING.  I was stupid ... I had run into a gray dragon that
left scales and I had gotten an amulet of reflection, which I stupidly
left behind.  I should have had a backup outfit ready to go in case I
lost the PYEC (which I did), but I didn't, and so my only resort when
it was stolen was to use up some wishes.

Playing wishless was a lot of fun, though (and quite challenging).  Up
until the very end when I blew off wishless I had not found a BoH nor
anything better than +2 leather gloves.


